      <!-- PRICING & BILLING -->
      <div style="margin-bottom:56px;">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:32px;padding-bottom:16px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--border);">
          <span style="color:var(--blue);">01 &nbsp;</span>Pricing &amp; Billing
        </h2>
        <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:0;">

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Is there really no large design deposit? No hidden fees?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">There's no large design deposit or upfront build fee. Here's how it actually works: you sign a simple service agreement, make your first monthly payment of $175, and we immediately begin building your website. No $3,000–$5,000 due before a single page is designed — just your regular monthly payment to get started. The only potential third-party cost is a domain name if you don't already have one (typically $15–20/year, paid directly to a registrar). We'll be transparent about everything before we begin.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              What's included in the $175/month?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">Everything. Custom design, custom-coded development, website hosting, unlimited content updates, 24/7 emergency support, mobile-first responsive design, Google PageSpeed optimization, on-page SEO foundation, and security monitoring. Your domain always stays in your name — you register and own it, we never do. There are no add-ons or upsells. The one flat rate covers your complete web presence, managed by us, for as long as you're with us.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Why is there a 12-month minimum?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">Building a custom website takes significant time and skill. A comparable site built traditionally would cost $3,000–$5,000 upfront. We absorb that cost on your behalf so you can get started with just your first month's payment — but we need a 12-month commitment to make that work economically. Think of it like getting a new phone on a contract: the carrier subsidizes the upfront cost, and you commit to service for a period. After 12 months, you're month-to-month and can cancel anytime with 30 days' notice.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              What happens if I cancel before 12 months?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">If you cancel before completing the 12-month minimum, you'd owe the balance of what the site would have cost as a lump-sum purchase ($4,000), minus the monthly payments you've already made. For example, if you cancel at month 6, you'd owe $4,000 minus $900 (6 × $175) = $3,100. We're always transparent about this before you sign. We've built a great product and we're confident you'll stay — but we want you to know the terms going in.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Is there a contract to sign?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes — a simple service agreement that outlines the terms we've described here: $175/month, 12-month minimum, what's included, and what happens if you cancel. No pages of fine print, no gotcha clauses. We keep it plain and readable because we want you to understand exactly what you're agreeing to.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Can I buy out my website instead of subscribing monthly?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. Our lump-sum purchase option is $4,000 upfront, and you own the code outright. Content updates are billed at $100/hour. This option is best for businesses that prefer a one-time investment. Contact us to discuss which option makes more sense for your situation.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- THE WEBSITE -->
      <div style="margin-bottom:56px;">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:32px;padding-bottom:16px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--border);">
          <span style="color:var(--blue);">02 &nbsp;</span>Your Website
        </h2>
        <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:0;">

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              How long does it take to build and launch my site?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">Most sites are live within 2–3 weeks. The process starts with a discovery call, then we design, build, and present your site for approval. Once you sign off, we launch. The biggest factor affecting timeline is how quickly you can provide us with your content — logo, photos, and the text you'd like on your pages. The sooner you get that to us, the sooner you're live.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              How many pages does my site include?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">Your monthly subscription includes up to 10 pages — typically Home, About, Services, Contact, and more depending on your business. Need pages beyond 10? We can add them for $150 per page, one-time.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Do I own the website?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">With the monthly subscription, we own and host the code — you're licensing the website as part of the service. This is how we're able to build it with no large design deposit. If you cancel after 12 months and want to take the code, we can discuss a reasonable buyout. If you'd prefer to own from day one, our lump-sum option ($4,000) gives you full ownership of the code.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Can I update the site myself?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">You don't need to — and that's the whole point. Unlimited updates are included. Just email or call us whenever you need something changed and we'll handle it, usually within one business day. We want you completely out of the technical weeds. Want to add a blog so you can post updates yourself? We can add that for a one-time fee of $200.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              What if I already have a website?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">No problem. We'll build your new custom site, and once you approve it, we'll point your existing domain to it and get your new site live with minimal downtime. Your domain stays in your name throughout — you always own it. Your old site can stay up until your new one is ready to launch, so there's no gap in your online presence.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Can you add ecommerce or online booking to my site?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. We can integrate third-party booking systems (like Calendly, Acuity, or Square Appointments) and payment forms into your custom-coded site. For full ecommerce stores, we build on a custom foundation or integrate with Stripe depending on your needs. Contact us to discuss your specific requirements and we'll give you an honest assessment of what's involved.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- TECHNICAL -->
      <div style="margin-bottom:56px;">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:32px;padding-bottom:16px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--border);">
          <span style="color:var(--blue);">03 &nbsp;</span>Technical Questions
        </h2>
        <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:0;">

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Why don't you use WordPress?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">WordPress is the #1 target for hackers on the internet — over 90% of hacked websites run on it. Beyond security, WordPress sites are inherently slow because of plugin bloat and templating overhead. Page builders like Elementor and Divi produce messy, heavy code that tanks your Google PageSpeed score and frustrates visitors. We write every line of code by hand. The result is a site that loads in under a second, scores high on Google PageSpeed Insights, is extremely difficult to hack, and is completely unique to your business.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Will my site show up on Google?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">We build every site with a solid on-page SEO foundation: fast load times (Google's #1 ranking factor), clean semantic HTML, proper heading structure, meta descriptions, Open Graph tags, and clean URLs. We submit your sitemap to Google Search Console on launch day. Ranking competitively for keywords requires ongoing SEO work (which is a separate service), but you'll start with a technically perfect foundation that gives you every advantage.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              How fast will my site load?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">Our custom-coded sites consistently load in under 1 second and score high on Google PageSpeed Insights — both mobile and desktop. We optimize every image, write lean CSS and JavaScript, use modern web standards, and host on fast servers. A fast site doesn't just please Google — it keeps visitors from bouncing and makes your business look professional.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Who owns my domain name?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">You do — always. Your domain is registered in your name and stays that way. We never take ownership of your domain. If you already have one, we'll help you point it to your new site. If you need to register one, we'll guide you through that process, but you'll be the registrant and pay for it directly (typically $15–20/year). We handle the technical DNS configuration on our end once it's pointed to us.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">
              Is my site secure? What about HTTPS?
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. Every site we build uses HTTPS (SSL encryption) — that's the padlock you see in the browser bar. We include SSL certificate management in the monthly fee. Beyond that, our custom-coded sites are inherently more secure than WordPress sites because there are no plugins, no database, and no attack surface for common WordPress exploits. We also monitor uptime and alert ourselves the moment anything looks off.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

